\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Traders Say  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Behind Shekel's Weakening\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sara Toth Stub   \par \uc2 301 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 April 2013\par 10:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders said Tuesday that another \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have caused the shekel to weaken, while \uc2 the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely small in size so far, but they expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue buying dollars throughout the day.\par \par \uc2 A move by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been expected because the shekel has appreciated against the dollar in recent trading sessions to its strongest level since Sept. 2, 2011. Also, the dollar fell to below ILS3.60 against the shekel, the same rate at which the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier this month, traders said.\par \par \uc2 At 0822 GMT, the dollar was trading up at ILS3.593, having fallen to as low as ILS3.575 Monday.\par \par \uc2 Rony Gitlin, head of spot trading at Bank Leumi Le \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said that because \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was expected, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would probably have to purchase a larger amount of dollars to affect the shekel rate than it did earlier this month, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was more of a surprise. The last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  before that was in 2011.\par \par \uc2 The previous \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  totaled about $100 million, according to traders, although the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wouldn't confirm that amount.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  mainly to prevent the shekel from becoming too strong and hurting Israel's exports, a cornerstone of the economy, according to Mr. Gitlin.\par \par \uc2 The shekel has strengthened in recent weeks partly due to production starting at a large natural gas reserve in Israel, which has the potential to make Israel energy independent or an exporter of energy, bringing more money into the economy.\par \par \uc2 Write to Sara Toth Stub at realtimedesklondon@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 30, 2013 04:57 ET (08:57 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130430e94u001u6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
