\par\par \b \uc2 Israel shekel at 1-month low vs dollar ahead of rate decision\b0\par\par\uc2 336 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 2013\par 15:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, Feb 25 (Reuters) - Israel's shekel fell to its lowest in nearly a month against the dollar on Monday, ahead of a possible \uc2 Bank of Israel\uc2  interest rate cut and speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again.\par \par \uc2 The shekel was at 3.717 per dollar at 1430 GMT, compared with 3.710 on Friday when the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slipped 1 percent.\par \par \uc2 A Reuters poll found seven of 11 economists believe \uc2 the Bank of Israel\uc2  will stand pat later in the session (1530 GMT) but the market sees a 50-50 chance of a quarter-point reduction to 1.5 percent, which would be the third cut in five months.\par \par \uc2 The shekel reached a 15-month peak of 3.66 per dollar last week but dealers said significant dollar buying by foreign banks and local customers buoyed the dollar the past couple of sessions.\par \par \uc2 A dealer at \uc2 Israel Discount Bank\uc2  said that if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  holds rates on Monday, the shekel would likely appreciate again. He noted that some banks would also sell dollars if it reached 3.74-3.75 shekels.\par \par \uc2 Koon Chow, an emerging markets strategist at \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2 , said he had closed his trade recommendation of being long shekel.\par \par \uc2 "Our view on the shekel's fundamentals has moderated, reflecting the softening growth profile of the Israeli economy," he wrote in a note to clients on Monday. "This argues, at the very least, for waiting for cheaper/weaker levels before being long shekel again."\par \par \uc2 Chow noted that the shekel remains strong and is on a par with levels in mid-2011 - when \uc2 the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  - on a trade-weighted basis.\par \par \uc2 "\uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be very reluctant to re-initiate \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  but could certainly warn of action or other quantitative steps, which could weaken the shekel," he said.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Steven Scheer; Editing by Hugh Lawson)\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL-SHEKEL/ | ABN | D | GFN | M | DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130225e92p000ua\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
