\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-POLL-Bank of Israel still seen holding rates steady, but may be close call\b0\par\par\uc2 583 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 2013\par 16:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Repeats poll that ran on Feb. 21, with no changes)\par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM, Feb 21 (Reuters) - Gains in the shekel  have increased the chances of a \uc2 Bank of Israel\uc2  rate cut but most analysts still expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hold off for at least another month, a Reuters poll showed.\par \par \uc2  Seven of the 11 economists surveyed by Reuters expect the monetary policy committee (MPC) will keep the benchmark rate at 1.75 percent for a second straight month. The others foresee a quarter-point reduction to 1.5 percent.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will announce its decision on Monday at 5.30 pm (1530 GMT).\par \par \uc2  Minutes from the Jan. 28 decision showed the MPC was in no rush to lower rates further amid signs of economic and price stability and concerns over rising home prices. Policymakers noted that the level of pessimism in the economy had declined and no longer indicated a continued slowdown in activity.\par \par \uc2  Rafael Gozlan, chief economist at the IBI Investment House, said that while he expects at least one more rate cut in the next couple of months, the MPC would prefer to wait until Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu completes the building of a ruling coalition before adjusting rates again.\par \par \uc2  "It will be a close call," Gozlan said. "I wouldn't be surprised if they do or don't go but I would be surprised if they don't cut in one of the next two meetings."\par \par \uc2  Much depends on how concerned \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials are over the shekel's appreciation to 3.67 per dollar, its strongest level since November 2011. \par \par \uc2  Analysts noted that more importantly, the shekel has also risen more than 2 percent on a trade weighted basis since the last rate decision. With exports - which account for more than 40 percent of Israel's economic activity, slowing - exporters want action by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has also raised speculation of a resumption of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  posted a budget deficit of 39 billion shekels in 2012, a much higher than planned 4.2 percent of gross domestic product. To meet a 3 percent target in 2013, the government will need to make steep spending cuts and hike taxes, according to \uc2 the Bank of Israel\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  Those who expect a rate cut next week point to a series of weak economic numbers in the past week. The annual inflation rate edged down to 1.5 percent in January as local demand remained weak; fourth-quarter GDP grew at an annualised rate of 2.5 percent for its slowest pace in 3-1/2 years and industrial production slid in December.\par \par \uc2  The economy grew 3.2 percent in 2012 and should grow 2.8 percent in 2013 excluding the start to natural gas production.\par \par \uc2  Analysts also believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has largely given up in its fight against rising home prices. It tightened mortgage regulations this week in a move analysts believe could pave the way for further rate cuts without worrying about home costs.\par \par \uc2  "Current economic data and soft inflation are rate-cut supportive," said \uc2 HSBC\uc2 's Murat Ulgen in a client note. "In light of recent economic data and measures taken by \uc2 the Bank of Israel\uc2  regarding mortgages, next week's rate decision could go either way but we are leaning in a direction of a rate cut." \par \par \uc2 (Editing by Jeremy Gaunt.)\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL-RATES/POLL | ABN | M | D | E | RBN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130228e92p0012r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
