\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Israel faces major budget challenge, says cbank\b0\par\par\uc2 579 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 2013\par 10:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Cbank forecasts higher-than-target 2013 budget deficit\par \par \uc2 * Cbank head Fischer says budget a priority for new government\par \par \uc2 * Suggests bank may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if strong shekel keeps rising\par \par \uc2 (Recasts with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Fischer's comments)\par \par \uc2 By Ari Rabinovitch\par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, Feb 13 (Reuters) - Israel's incoming government faces a major task to keep public finances in order, the head of its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday, while dropping hints the bank may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken a strong shekel.\par \par \uc2 "It must be the hope of the government, of the prime minister, to get the budget in shape immediately. And that's something which would certainly benefit the country," \uc2 Stanley Fischer\uc2  told reporters.\par \par \uc2 "Whether it will be politically possible is something we'll have to wait and see," he said, as \uc2 the Bank of Israel\uc2  forecast a higher-than-target 2013 deficit of at least 3.6 percent of gross domestic product.\par \par \uc2 Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu, who was narrowly reelected in a Jan. 22 vote that had been brought forward because his previous government was unable to pass a 2013 budget, is still negotiating with potential coalition partners.\par \par \uc2 His party won 31 seats in the 120-member parliament and he has until mid-March to cobble together a new coalition.\par \par \uc2 Once formed, it will have to fill a budget hole that in 2012 ballooned to nearly 40 billion shekels ($11 billion), mostly due to lower than expected tax income. In GDP terms, that translates to 4.2 percent, more than double an initial aim.\par \par \uc2 "There are no easy solutions to this problem. In such cases there is frequently a temptation to kick the can down the road. We've seen that in other countries," Fischer said.\par \par \uc2 The budget deficit could jump to as high as 4.9 percent of GDP if the state does not cut spending or raise taxes, or 3.6 percent without tax hikes, \uc2 the Bank of Israel\uc2  said in a statement. The finance ministry's forecast is 3 percent.\par \par \uc2 The bank based its deficit prediction on 3.8 percent growth rate, and Fischer said Israel's economy remained strong in comparison to the rest of the world.\par \par \uc2 That rate includes natural gas production set to begin in a few months at a newly discovered off-shore field.\par \par \uc2 SHEKEL \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 Tapping into an increasingly fraught global debate about competitive devaluations, Fischer said \uc2 the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to weaken the shekel if it strengthened further.\par \par \uc2 Noting the shekel has been rising as other countries keep their interest rates low in comparison to Israel's 1.75 percent benchmark, he told reporters: "More money started coming into Israel to take advantage of the small differential...\par \par \uc2 "That's something we're going to have to watch."\par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the shekel in the past to protect the economy, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now at a 15-month high against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Fischer's comment on Wednesday offered the clearest indication since last month - when he made similar remarks to Reuters Television at Davos - that it may do so again.\par \par \uc2 The strength of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has weighed on exporters, who account for 40 percent of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economic activity and have urged \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 3.69 shekels)\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Steven Scheer; Editing by John Stonestreet)\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL-CENBANK/BUDGET (PIX, UPDATE 2) | ABN | D | GFN | M | E | RBN | RNP | DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130213e92d000ob\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
