\par\par \b \uc2 REFILE-Eyes turn to \uc2 Bank of Israel\uc2  as shekel gains vs dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 By Steven Scheer   \par \uc2 867 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Februar 2013\par 10:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Corrects title of Modi Shafrir to head of research)\par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, Feb 5 (Reuters) - Israel's shekel is at a 15-month high against the dollar, prompting speculation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market that \uc2 the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it has in the past to protect the economy.\par \par \uc2 But the shekel may have to strengthen quite a lot further and against a broader range of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to convince the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to act again.\par \par \uc2 While some nations have complained about countries such as Japan seeking to boost growth through money-printing that also holds down the value of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Israel has avoided taking a stand on the issue internationally.\par \par \uc2 It \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the shekel over more than three years up to July 2011, buying some $50 billion of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in an effort that also boosted its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to nearly $80 billion.\par \par \uc2 Since then, the shekel had gradually depreciated from 3.4 per dollar to a low of 4.08 last July, making \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unnecessary.\par \par \uc2 But despite factors that should be crimping the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value - an announcement last week that Bank of Israel Governor \uc2 Stanley Fischer\uc2  was stepping down in June two years ahead of time, interest rate cuts and the constant worry of tensions on Israel's Syrian and Lebanese borders - the shekel is now back to a rate of about 3.69 per dollar, its strongest level since November 2011.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts believe the shekel's appreciation may prompt the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to resume its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases soon.\par \par \uc2 "We are getting close to (\uc2 the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market again," said Modi Shafrir, head of research at ILS Brokers. "We still have room - 3.60 or maybe less. But if the appreciation continues, they will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's focus will be mainly on the shekel's value against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that include the dollar, euro, yen and sterling. That basket is trading at 89, compared with 95 last July and just above a level of 86 the last time the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Shafrir says that since late July, when the shekel weakened to 4.08 per dollar, it has appreciated about 9 percent, significantly more than a 2.3 percent average among emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the MSCI index.\par \par \uc2 Much still depends on how \uc2 the Bank of Israel\uc2  views the shekel's relative strength.\par \par \uc2 "The correlation is very high between the dollar-shekel and euro-dollar," said Rony Gitlin, head of spot trading at Bank Leumi, attributing the shekel's strength against the dollar partly to the euro's strength.\par \par \uc2 Against the euro, the shekel rate of 5.0 is in the middle of a range of roughly 4.9-5.1 seen in recent years.\par \par \uc2 "They need the euro-shekel to be a few percent lower before they even start to think about it," Gitlin said. "There is no reason to buy dollars. Israel is part of the world so if the dollar is down around the world, it's the same here."\par \par \uc2 Noting that euro-shekel rate was 4.85 and the euro near $1.50 when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he added: "The only way they will buy is if there is a failure in the market," referring to the shekel's surge in value in March 2008.\par \par \uc2 STRONG ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Israel\uc2  has not officially declared an end to the policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  it began then and pursued until July 2011.\par \par \uc2 "We've said we will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when we think the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is away from its fundamental value. That remains our policy," Fischer told Reuters Television last month in Davos. "We haven't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at all in a year and a half. We hope we don't have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but if we have to, we will."\par \par \uc2 In lowering its benchmark interest rate in recent months, \uc2 the Bank of Israel\uc2  cited the need to weaken the shekel to help exports, which account for about 40 percent of economic activity. Weaker exports led Israel's economy to slow to 3.3 percent growth in 2012 from 4.6 percent in 2011.\par \par \uc2 Investors have been encouraged by Israel's election results from last month that signal a less aggressive foreign policy and a high chance that the new coalition government can agree on keeping the budget under control.\par \par \uc2 The shekel's strength also reflects the prospects of Israel starting natural gas production in April or May, Shafrir said. Israel's economy is projected to grow 2.8 percent in 2013, or 3.5-3.8 percent including natural gas output.\par \par \uc2 While a bounce in euro-dollar has contributed to a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Gaelle Blanchard, an emerging markets strategist at \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2 , believes some investors see the shekel as a defensive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the context of crises elsewhere.\par \par \uc2 Even so, she sees the shekel's rally near its end, strengthening no further than 3.60-3.65 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Ruth Pitchford)\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL-SHEKEL/  (REFILE) | C | D | E | M | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | ABX | BNX | FUN | RNA   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130209e9260002r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
