\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ Israeli Finance Minister "Comfortable" With Recent Shekel Weakness\b0\par\par\uc2 482 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 2012\par 16:49\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 13 Nov 2012 10:53 EDT *DJ  Finance Minister: \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  May \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to Support Shekel\par \par \uc2 13 Nov 2012 10:56 EDT DJ  Israeli Finance Minister "Comfortable" With Recent Shekel Weakness\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Sara Toth Stub \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JERUSALEM--Israeli Finance Minister Yuval Steinitz said Tuesday that he is "comfortable" with the recent weakening of the shekel against the U.S. dollar, noting that it has provided a much-needed boost to the country's exports.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But Mr. Steinitz indicated that the Israeli \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if it falls much further.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We prefer not to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but we don't want to see it extremely weakened either," he told Dow Jones Newswires in an interview.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We have a problem of high prices," Mr. Steinitz added, and a sharply weaker \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could increase living costs for Israelis, a highly sensitive issue in a country which saw large public protests last year over rising costs.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Israeli shekel has weakened about 6% against the dollar over the last year, trading at ILS3.9265 against the dollar Tuesday, a three-year low.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At times in 2011 the shekel traded as strong as ILS3.3 against the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been hurt by the rise in Israel's budget and current-account deficits, as well as concerns about geopolitical threats, most notably from Iran, which Israel fears is developing nuclear weapons. Regime change in Egypt has also added to strategic concerns. More recently, the dollar has strengthened on global markets following the re-election of U.S. President Barack Obama.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mr. Steinitz said the recent weakening in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been good for Israel's exports, a cornerstone of the economy. "I feel quite comfortable with the current level [of the shekel]," Mr. Steinitz said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Israeli exports rose 2.5% on the month in October, to total $4.43 billion, after rising 3% on the month in September, according to the Central Bureau of Statistics. Exports are on track to grow 8.4% on the year in 2012, according to estimates from the statistics bureau.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Any \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would be a turnaround from last year, when the Israeli \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tried to weaken the shekel by purchasing millions of dollars on the open market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 And in a bid to stop what it said were speculative purchases of the Israeli \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the government increased taxes and imposed new restrictions on bond and shekel transactions by foreigners.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  and the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development\f28 \uc2 \f2  criticized the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , saying the policy was artificial and couldn't be sustained, and might serve to deter foreign investors.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Sara Toth Stub at realtimedesklondon@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Subscribe to WSJ: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 November 13, 2012 10:56 ET (15:56 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020121113e8bd004gp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw145\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2175\pichgoal600
