\par\par \b \uc2 OIL FUTURES: Crude Rallies As Fed  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Seen\b0\par\par\uc2 523 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 August 2011\par 18:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global News Select\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 --Easy-money hopes lift futures\par \par \uc2 --Jitters as \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  sends two warships to Red Sea border with Egypt\par \par \uc2 --Attention to shift to Fed minutes due later Tuesday\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Dan Strumpf \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW YORK -(Dow Jones)- Oil futures pushed higher Tuesday on expectations that the Federal Reserve will continue its easy-money policy, while reports of Israeli warships near Egypt kept traders on guard.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Light, sweet crude for October delivery rose $1.39, or 1.6%, to $88.66 barrel on the \f28 \uc2 \f2 New York Mercantile Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Brent crude on the ICE Futures Europe exchange traded up $1.94, or 1.7%, to $113.82 a barrel.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Futures were higher in thin volume as traders honed in on comments from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve Bank of Chicago\f28 \uc2 \f2  President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Charles Evans\f28 \uc2 \f2 , who said the economy is moving "sideways" and could use assistance from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I would favor more accommodation," Evans told CNBC during an interview on Tuesday, raising expectations that the Fed could engage in another round of monetary stimulus. Such stimulus weakens the dollar, which in turn tends to boost oil prices by making the dollar-denominated commodity cheaper for holders of other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders will get additional insight into the Fed's thinking later Tuesday when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  releases minutes from the Federal Open Market Committee's Aug. 9 meeting.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "[The minutes] are likely to show a divisive debate over QE3 and could increase market sentiment that another stimulus is coming," said Jason Schenker, president of Austin, Texas, consultancy Prestige Economics.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A move by the equity markets into positive territory also helped power futures higher. The Dow Jones Industrial Average was up 0.1% to 11,555.6 after trading in the red earlier in the session.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oil futures in recent weeks have closely mirrored movements in major U.S. equity indices, which many traders have come to see as barometers of sentiment about the broader economy. Cracks in the fragile U.S. recovery have sent both equities and crude prices sliding in recent months, with Nymex futures coming off a high of nearly $115 a barrel in May.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Still, traders continue to keep an eye on events overseas. Some oil brokers said reports that Israel had sent two warships to the Red Sea border with Egypt was raising concerns about the prospect of additional conflict in the Middle East.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The warships were dispatched following warnings that militants were planning an attack on southern Israel from Egyptian soil, according to the Associated Press.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Market participants are also keeping close watch on Libya for hints on when production and exports would restart. On Monday, Libya's rebel-controlled \f28 \uc2 \f2 Arabian Gulf Oil Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said it plans to restart production and exports by the end of September.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Front-month September reformulated gasoline blendstock, or RBOB, recently traded up 6.61 cents, or 2.3%, to $2.9725 a gallon. September heating oil gained 5.83 cents, or 1.9%, to $3.0685 a gallon.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Dan Strumpf, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2818; dan.strumpf@dowjones.com. [ 08-30-11 1234ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1086 28028 28031 4107  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020110830e78u0004f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
