\par\par \b \uc2 INTERVIEW-UPDATE 1-Prices under control, trend unclear- \highlight22\uc2 Israel \highlight\uc2  cbank\b0\par\par\uc2 By Steven Scheer and Sebastian Tong   \par \uc2 667 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juli 2011\par 15:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds Fischer comments, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 LONDON, July 7 (Reuters) - Inflation expectations in \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  are being held down but it remains to be seen if stable oil and food prices will be sustainable, said Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Stanley Fischer on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to Reuters Insider TV on the sidelines of an investor conference in London, Fischer said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to remain flexible on its interest policy as the global outlook was still murky.\par \par \uc2 "Inflation has tamped down in part because we raised interest rates a lot. More importantly, energy prices have come down and food prices stabilised somewhat. Two of the causes of Israeli inflation have changed direction. Whether this is temporary we don't know," Fischer said.\par \par \uc2 Fischer earlier told the conference that high housing prices remained a key concern for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that policymakers would continue to act to rein in housing costs.\par \par \uc2 "We are seeing a slowdown in the rate of increase in housing prices but the rate of the increase is still too high ... We will continue to work gradually to bring this under control reasonably soon," Fischer said.\par \par \uc2 "If there's something like a bubble, you don't want to take a heavy hammer and explode the whole thing. We have consciously taken serious measures ... to try and slow the rate of increase and not kill the market completely," he said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has taken a number of measures to cool the property market, including raising interest rates. Rising rapidly since 2008, Israeli home prices have surged some 50 percent in three years.\par \par \uc2 After 10 interest rate hikes since August 2009, the Bank of Israel left its benchmark lending rate steady at 3.25 percent at its monthly policy meeting last week, citing concerns over the U.S. economy and the European debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 "We make interest rate decisions once a month because we need time to see what's happening in the global economy. We have noticed in the last few weeks that the (economic) sentiment is changing favourably, certainly in Israel, and maybe elsewhere as well. But we're still looking at a very unclear picture," he said.\par \par \uc2 But Israeli exports, which had helped drive economic growth in 2010, had underperformed in the last three months. Fischer said it was uncertain whether this was a result of the strength of the shekel or due to weak global demand.\par \par \uc2 "We'll have to analyse this to see what's causing this change," he said.\par \par \uc2 Financial markets and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's own economists project another one percentage point of tightening in the next year but when asked if that still held true, Fischer said it was possible that outlook could change should the global economy stay weak.\par \par \uc2 He said the European debt crisis was not yet affecting Israel's economy but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was watching developments closely since one third of Israel's exports go to Europe.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it bought $425 million in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June, more than double the $200 million in May, to curb the shekel's strength.\par \par \uc2 "We prefer not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and we don't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless we think the market is going to places that are not consistent with where we think the equilibrium should be. We're \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  less than we did two years ago and less than we did a year ago and we hope gradually to go down to zero," he said.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time in more than a month, buying tens of millions of dollars as the shekel headed towards 3.40 per dollar for a three-week peak. Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared to be trying to keep dollar-shekel, which had strengthened to 3.46 last week, above 3.40.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Nick Edwards)\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Susan Fenton)\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL-FISCHER/ (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110710e777000cx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
