\par\par \b \uc2 INTERVIEW- \highlight22\uc2 Israel \highlight\uc2  cbank wants to avoid  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2 -Fischer\b0\par\par\uc2 716 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Mai 2011\par 13:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  cbank head sees 4.5-5 pct economic growth in 2011\par \par \uc2 * Fischer: Israel is essentially at full employment\par \par \uc2 * Fischer: Main priority on housing is halt price rises\par \par \uc2 * Fischer: IMF head should not have to be European\par \par \uc2 PARIS, May 25 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  prefers not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market but will do so if the shekel <ILS=> strengthens significantly, Governor Stanley Fischer said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Israel's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief also projected Israel's economy would grow by 4.5 to 5 percent this year as exports remain strong.\par \par \uc2 "We have been pleasantly surprised by the behaviour of exports and we don't see any problem in the area of exports at current exchange rates," Fischer, a former first managing director of the International Monetary Fund (IMF), told Reuters Insider TV on the sidelines of the OECD forum in Paris.\par \par \uc2 "If the exchange rate were to move dramatically, we would probably have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again but of course, we would always prefer not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if we can avoid it," he added.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Israel has bought tens of billions of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  the past three years in part to prevent damage to local exporters since exports account for more than 40 percent of Israel's economic activity.\par \par \uc2 It bought $1.495 billion of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  in April but purchases so far in May were small amid news that exports continue to grow despite the strong shekel, which is near a three-year peak versus the dollar. Exports grew 16 percent in the first quarter.\par \par \uc2 Fischer also said inflation, at an annual rate of 4 percent in April, was too high and required the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise its benchmark rate by a quarter-point to 3.25 percent on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The hike was the fourth in five months and 10th in the current cycle.\par \par \uc2 "Our inflation rate has eased but it is still significantly above the 3 percent upper limit of our target range and is expected to stay there," Fischer said, adding inflation would fall back below a 3 percent rate within a year.\par \par \uc2 "We are essentially at full employment now," he said, referring to a jobless rate of 6 percent. "We are growing very fast and the major threats we would face are in the direction of inflation."\par \par \uc2 HOUSING BUBBLE\par \par \uc2 One key concern for policymakers has been soaring housing prices and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has acted to try and limit price gains. Fischer said the Bank of Israel does not want to burst the bubble.\par \par \uc2 "We want to reduce the pressure in the market gradually and we think we are doing that," he said. "Whether prices will go down is not entirely clear at this stage but the first priority is to stop them from going up."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had previously indicated it would likely raise its 2011 estimate from a current forecast of 4.5 percent but Fischer declined to say to what level.\par \par \uc2 "I expect we will raise it but not by a huge amount," Fischer said. He noted that while Israel has grown an average of 5 percent since 2003 except during the recession, "I am not sure whether we can get there. We may be somewhere in the range of 4.5 to 5 percent, which would be very good in terms of increasing employment."\par \par \uc2 Fischer has been mentioned as a possible replacement to head the IMF but he declined to say whether he has been approached about the job.\par \par \uc2 "It's one of the best jobs in the international system but I have a terrific job at the moment. It matters to me what happens in Israel," Fischer said.\par \par \uc2 However, he said the convention of choosing an IMF chief must change.\par \par \uc2 "We have been told repeatedly it is about to change," Fischer said. "Saying it doesn't have to be a European doesn't mean it cannot be a European if they are the best candidate.\par \par \uc2 "I hope we will take away the geographical presumption," he said. "I thought we had already done that but apparently not."\par \par \uc2 Watch the Reuters Insider TV interview\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/mev69r"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/mev69r}}}\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Axel Threlfall, Writing by Steven Scheer)\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL-FISCHER/ (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110528e75p000bj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
