\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Israel \highlight\uc2  shekel jumps 1.1 pct, prompts  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Steven Scheer   \par \uc2 410 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Mai 2011\par 16:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, May 19 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's shekel gained 1.1 percent against the dollar in heavy trade on Thursday as the market positioned for a possible interest rate rise next week, prompting \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise.\par \par \uc2 "We saw a lot of sellers (of dollars) -- hundreds of millions from offshore banks and hedge funds," said a dealer at Bank Leumi.\par \par \uc2 The shekel recovered losses seen earlier in the week as some analysts say the Bank of Israel may opt to raise rates at a meeting on Monday now that the shekel has weakened from a near three-year peak of 3.38 rate last month. Others believe the bank can wait since inflation pressures have eased along with sliding commodities prices.\par \par \uc2 The shekel <ILS=> was fixed at a one-week high of 3.49 per dollar, compared with 3.5290 on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 It later firmed to 3.4820, prompting the Bank of Israel to buy about $100 million of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the rise, dealers said. It was the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in more than two weeks.\par \par \uc2 The shekel moved back to 3.4940 per dollar in late trading.\par \par \uc2 It had been trading around 3.54 over the past three sessions as data on inflation and economic growth were a bit weaker than expected, prompting economists to lower the chances of a rate increase next week.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said there was heavy dollar buying by hedge funds and foreign banks over the prior three sessions.\par \par \uc2 In a Reuters poll, 12 of 21 forecast the Bank of Israel will leave its key rate at 3 percent for a second straight month. The other nine expect a 25 basis point increase. [ID:nLDE74I0TN]\par \par \uc2 Israel's consumer price index rose a less-than-expected 0.6 percent in April from March, while the annual rate eased to 4 percent from 4.3 percent in March. [ID:nJES000060]\par \par \uc2 Inflation expectations for the next year based on bond yields fell to 3.1 percent in April from 3.7 percent in March. [ID:nLDE74H19I]\par \par \uc2 First-quarter gross domestic product grew by an annualised 4.7 percent, slightly below forecasts of 5 percent growth, and a slowdown from a 7.6 percent expansion in the fourth quarter of 2010. [ID:nLDE74F122]\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Susan Fenton)\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL-SHEKEL/ (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110522e75j000ew\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
