\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Israel \highlight\uc2 's Fischer: Hope Level Of  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\uc2  Will Be Minimal\b0\par\par\uc2 675 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 April 2011\par 11:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 28 Apr 2011 05:00 EDT *DJ  \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Fischer: Don't Know What \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Levels Will Be\par \par \uc2 28 Apr 2011 05:00 EDT *DJ  Israel's Fischer: Exports Doing Well Despite \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Appreciation\par \par \uc2 28 Apr 2011 05:00 EDT *DJ  Israel's Fischer: 'Promising' Outlook For Israeli Economy\par \par \uc2 28 Apr 2011 05:00 EDT DJ  Bank Of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Fischer: Hope Level Of \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Will Be Minimal\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Anjali Cordeiro \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Israel's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor, Stanley Fischer, said in an interview that the bank hopes its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets will need to be minimal, although the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remains ready to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if it feels the shekel's value isn't appropriate.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Israeli \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , like policymakers in other growing economies, has recently shown more tolerance for a stronger \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as it fights inflation. Fischer acknowledged the bank's recent willingness to accept a stronger shekel, pointing to its interest rate hikes earlier this year and to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent rise.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We don't know what the level of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is going to be. We hope it will be minimal," Fischer said. But he warned that if the shekel starts to move in directions that aren't in keeping with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's estimates of where the market and the economy are then "we will have to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ." Fischer said the bank doesn't publish its views on the equilibrium levels for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Israel recently raised its economic growth forecast to 4.5%. On Wednesday Fischer said he wouldn't be surprised if in the first quarter "we grew faster than that."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Over the last two years, the Israeli \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to keep a lid on the shekel. It has done so by buying dollars and by building up its reserves. On Sunday, the bank said that it was keeping its interest rate unchanged, at 3%, while pointing to the rising value of the shekel against the U.S. dollar and to a lower-than-expected 0.2% consumer price index increase in March. The bank suggested that the appreciation of the shekel could help curb inflation. In late March, the bank had raised its interest rate by 50 basis points.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Israeli economy is doing "very well," Fischer said, noting that exports have done well despite the appreciation in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . In its recent interest rate statement, the bank estimated that the shekel appreciated by 3.7% against the dollar from its monetary policy decision held on March 27 through April 20. The Israeli \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was recently near ILS3.424 per dollar Wednesday, according to CQG.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It's a promising outlook, but we know we live in an uncertain world so you have to stay on your guard all the time," he said. Fischer acknowledged the uncertainty created by the political upheaval in the Middle East. "There is a lot more uncertainty than there used to be," he said. "We've got to be prepared for a greater variety of scenarios."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fischer didn't comment on the Fed's quantitative easing program, which is due to end in June, but he said that as and when developed nations start moving to a tighter monetary policy some of the upward pressure on emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might ease, although that is unlikely to be soon.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I'm sure when interest rate relationships return to normal, which is not going to happen overnight, then because of capital flows, exchange rates will adjust," he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fischer is seen as an influential voice in global financial markets, partly because of his role in helping manage the Asian financial crisis in the late 1990s, when he was the International Monetary Fund's second-in-command.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Anjali Cordeiro; Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2200; anjali.cordeiro@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 April 28, 2011 05:00 ET (09:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020110428e74s002f3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw77\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1155\pichgoal600
