\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Shekel at 2-1/2-yr high;  \highlight22\uc2 Israel \highlight\uc2  cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 408 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 April 2011\par 13:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Shekel fixed at 3.4170 per dollar\par \par \uc2 * Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  buys $100 mln, dealers say\par \par \uc2 (Adds details, shekel fixing rate, dealer comments)\par \par \uc2 By Steven Scheer\par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, April 13 (Reuters) - Israel's shekel <ILS=> advanced to a fresh 2-1/2-year high against the dollar in subdued trading on Wednesday, prompting \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  to try to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains.\par \par \uc2 "I didn't see anyone else buying (dollars) but the Bank of Israel," said a dealer at \uc2 Israel Discount Bank\uc2 . "There is no liquidity on the upside. People are expecting another rate hike so there is no reason to buy dollars."\par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought an estimated $100 million of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "They bought $100 million and it disappeared," the dealer said. "Offshore banks sold $200 million."\par \par \uc2 The shekel was fixed at 3.4170 per dollar -- its strongest level since Sept. 25, 2008 -- compared with 3.4460 on Tuesday. It gained to 3.4140 to the dollar after the fixing.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought nearly $50 billion of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past three years, including $2.5 billion since the beginning of 2011.\par \par \uc2 A senior Bank of Israel official told Reuters on Tuesday that the bank's eventual exit from the market will be gradual and partly hinges on the pace of U.S. and European interest rate increases. He also said that, at 3 percent, interest rates in Israel were still low. [ID:nLDE73B1NV] [ID:nLDE73B15U]\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Israel raised its key rate by a more than expected half point on March 28, its ninth move since August 2009. The market expects one further point of tightening in 2011 but players are split as to whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will raise rates again on April 24.\par \par \uc2 Also lifting the shekel on Wednesday was the euro's move to a 15-month high against the dollar, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 Dealers noted that liquidity was very low heading into the seven-day Jewish festival of Passover, which starts at sundown on Monday. Thursday will be the last full day of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading until April 26.\par \par \uc2 Data earlier in the session showed that Israel's foreign trade deficit widened to $1.23 billion in March from $992 million in February and $234 million in March 2010. [ID:nLDE73C10F]\par \par \uc2 (Editing by John Stonestreet)\par \par \uc2 SHEKEL-\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110413e74d000ok\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
