\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Israel's GDP Grows An Annualized 7.8% In 4Q\b0\par\par\uc2 252 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Februar 2011\par 17:11\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Adds details of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  move.\par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM (Dow Jones)--Israel's gross domestic product grew at an annualized rate of 7.8% in the fourth quarter, its statistics bureau said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 In the third quarter, annualized growth was only 4.4%. In the second half of the year, GDP grew 5.4%, down from 5.6% in the first half, due mainly to the slower third quarter, the bureau said.\par \par \uc2 The growth was fueled by an increase in exports and private consumption, especially of durable goods, according to the figures. For all of 2010, GDP grew an estimated 4%, after increasing 0.8% in 2009, the bureau said. The figures for 2010 are based on preliminary data.\par \par \uc2 The Israeli shekel initially appreciated sharply against the dollar after the data was released, but eased off when the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise, according to a London-based person close to the matter.\par \par \uc2 At 1551 GMT, the dollar was trading at ILS3.609 against the Israeli shekel after moving as low as ILS3.603 before the bank was suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Over the past two years, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on a number of occasions to stem the shekel's strength and keep exports competitive.\par \par \uc2 -By Sara Toth Stub, Contributing to Dow Jones Newswires, saratoth@gmail.com\par \par \uc2 (Clare Connaghan in London contributed to this report.) [ 02-16-11 1111ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110216e72g000ch\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
