ect To Raise Economic Growth Forecast For 2011\par \par \uc2 12 Feb 2011 06:23 EDT *DJ  Bank Of Israel Gov: Rate Of Increase Of Housing Prices Has Been "Very Fast"\par \par \uc2 12 Feb 2011 06:23 EDT *DJ  Bank Of Israel Gov: May See "Bubble Like" Situation If House Prices Keep Growing Fast\par \par \uc2 12 Feb 2011 06:24 EDT *DJ  Bank Of Israel Gov: Won't Hesitate To Act On Housing Prices If Needed\par \par \uc2 12 Feb 2011 06:25 EDT *DJ  Bank Of Israel Gov: Current Estimates Show Housing Prices Not Too Far From Equilibrium\par \par \uc2 12 Feb 2011 06:25 EDT *DJ  Bank Of Israel Gov: To Take Higher Asset Prices Into Consideration For Rate Moves\par \par \uc2 12 Feb 2011 06:25 EDT *DJ  Bank Of Israel Gov: Lower Interest Rates Contributing To Higher Asset Prices\par \par \uc2 12 Feb 2011 06:25 EDT *DJ  Bank Of Israel Gov: Open To Taking Macro-Prudential Measures On Housing\par \par \uc2 12 Feb 2011 06:42 EDT DJ  Bank Of Israel Gov:Govt Should Stick To Budget Deficit Target\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--The Israeli government should stick to its budget deficit aim as the current political uncertainty in the Middle East may linger after the fall of Egyptian President Hosni Mubarak from power, its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said, days after the government announced measures to stave off popular protest.\par \par \uc2 "As a central banker, I have no comments on the political situation, but in light of the increased uncertainty it is more important than ever that we manage both fiscal policy and monetary policy very well," Bank Of Israel Governor Stanley Fischer told Dow Jones Newswires in an interview Saturday.\par \par \uc2 Thursday, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's government announced measures worth NIS2.2 million for 2011-2012 spread equally over two years following public outrage over the wave of price increases in the economy.\par \par \uc2 Israel's budget deficit stood at 3.7% in 2010. The government has ambitious plans to bring it down the budget deficit to 3% in 2011.\par \par \uc2 "Once you said that I am going to do 3% then your credibility depends on doing 3%. What's important is maintaining the credibility of Israeli economic policy," Fischer said.\par \par \uc2 --By Subhadip Sircar & Khushita Vasant; Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 61456113; subhadip.sircar@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 February 12, 2011 06:42 ET (11:42 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020110212e72c0013b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw77\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1155\pichgoal600
