\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Israel cbank sees  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  buying as "essential" -minutes\b0\par\par\uc2 651 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Februar 2011\par 11:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Jan. 24 rate hike supported by all 4 cenbank officials\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  "essential, should continue"\par \par \uc2 * Housing prices likely to gain further in 2011\par \par \uc2 * Global economy improving\par \par \uc2 (Adds details, comments)\par \par \uc2 By Steven Scheer\par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, Feb 7 (Reuters) - The Bank of Israel has decided that it would continue a nearly three-year policy of buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the shekel <ILS=> from appreciating rapidly, minutes of a Jan. 24 rates decision showed on Monday.\par \par \uc2 In the meeting that ended with a quarter-point increase in the benchmark rate <ILINR=ECI> to 2.25 percent, the question came up whether there was a need for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, and if so, what degree was required.\par \par \uc2 "Discussion focused particularly on how much flexibility the exchange rate should be allowed, and the implications of various scenarios on the trade balance and on capital flows. It was agreed that in light of the developments on the real side during 2010, the Bank of Israel's policy ... was still essential and should continue," the minutes said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  started \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market in March 2008 with $25 million a day, a level that rose to $100 million four months later. Since August 2009, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been on days the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  deems necessary.\par \par \uc2 It bought $2.085 billion of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in January after buying $1.815 billion in December.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Israel, which has made slowing the shekel's rise central to its monetary policy, has bought tens of billions of dollars over the past three years but the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stayed strong, partly due to a wide interest rates gap with the United States and Europe -- Israel's main trading partners.\par \par \uc2 Some officials expressed fears of a further appreciation of the shekel should the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raise rates. But new \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  directives [ID:nLDE70J1KN] aimed at moderating the effects of wider interest rate differentials on the shekel allowed the rate hike to proceed, the minutes said.\par \par \uc2 Bank of Israel Governor Stanley Fischer's decision to raise the key rate was supported by all four \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials. The increase was the first such move in four months and the seventh time since August 2009. The current interest rate is deemed expansionary, the bank said.\par \par \uc2 INFLATION\par \par \uc2 Inflation, according to the bond market and economists, is expected to remain at 3 percent or above for most of 2011, higher than an annual target of 1-3 percent. That, the minutes said, "indicate the need for an increase in the interest rate."\par \par \uc2 Israel had inflation 2.7 percent in 2010, much of that stemming from gains in housing costs, an issue that was a major challenge for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year.\par \par \uc2 House prices rose 17 percent in 2010 as low interest rates led to a rapid expansion of housing credit, while housing demand outpaced supply. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials agreed "there was a significant probability that housing prices would continue their rapid rate of increase in the coming year".\par \par \uc2 In addition to interest rate hikes, the Bank of Israel has already taken a number of steps aimed at raising banks' mortgage loan rates. Policymakers said they would introduce further measures "if there was no change in the path of prices and in the degree of leverage".\par \par \uc2 Also supporting a rate increase last month was Israel's "substantial expansion" of the economy and employment levels. After growing 4.5 percent in 2010, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sees strong growth continuing in the first quarter of 2011, which would boost inflation, the minutes said.\par \par \uc2 "It was also noted that the most recent data indicate more positive assessments of the recovery of the global economy from the economic crisis," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Ron Askew)\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL-RATES/MINUTES (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|BNX|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110207e7270011r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
