\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  COLUMN-Israeli shekel might be worth a cautious look\b0\par\par\uc2 729 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 2011\par 12:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 -- Neal Kimberley is an \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market analyst for Reuters. The opinions expressed are his own --\par \par \uc2 By Neal Kimberley\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Feb 2 (Reuters) - With protesters still thronging the streets of Cairo and deep political uncertainty over the future of Egypt, this might not seem the best moment to buy the Israeli shekel <ILS=>.\par \par \uc2 But adventurous traders might conclude that the fall in the Jewish state's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar from 3.5130 on Jan. 18 to Wednesday's 3.6700 is overdone.\par \par \uc2 After all the abrupt slide in the shekel has rapidly taken it back to levels last seen in September with barely a pause.\par \par \uc2 The acceleration in shekel weakness since Thursday drove it to 3.75 per dollar on Monday and has mirrored the surge in popular unrest in neighbouring Egypt.\par \par \uc2 The 1979 peace treaty between the two countries has been a cornerstone of Israeli security for more than 30 years.\par \par \uc2 Yet there seems no indication so far that the popular calls for political change in Egypt include demands for a wholesale reassessment of the relationship with Israel.\par \par \uc2 So, although the political situation in Egypt and other Middle East and North African (MENA) countries is very fluid, a weakening of the shekel on geopolitical factors alone may have overshot.\par \par \uc2 Of course, traders will be aware that Israel's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has pushed against the strength of the shekel in recent months, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly to stem its rise.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $2.3 billion of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in December and on Jan. 20 imposed a reserve requirement on some \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  derivative deals. [ID:nLDE70J1KN]\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the finance ministry announced a proposal to tax profits on foreigners' investments in short-term debt -- another step to curb speculative inflows. [ID:nLDE70Q1HO] [ID:nLDE70J1KN]\par \par \uc2 Yet the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised interest rates on Jan. 24, saying inflation expectations for the coming 12 months had increased to 3 percent, the upper limit of its target range. [ID:nLDE70N1Y5]\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , noting imports into Israel rose 5 percent in December, said: "Inflationary pressures continue to mount in the emerging market economies, deriving from the steep increases in commodity prices in general, and food prices in particular."\par \par \uc2 Some might feel that continuing to seek a weakening of the shekel, especially in the face of the unrest-related sell-off, sits uncomfortably with an anti-inflationary strategy that recognises the threat of imported price pressures.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  acknowledged in minutes of its Dec. 27 meeting that the "appreciation of the shekel in the last few months had helped to moderate inflation". [ID:nLDE7090V3]\par \par \uc2 And while bank governor Stanley Fischer, speaking in Davos on Jan. 26, still thought the shekel was slightly too firm (USD/ILS was then around 3.62), the International Monetary Fund on Jan. 24 took a different tack on the value of continued \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  against shekel strength. [ID:nLDE70P29I] [ID:nSLAOCE7NE]\par \par \uc2 "Given that reserves and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sterilisation losses are already considerable, and that persistent one-sided use of this instrument undermines the credibility of the floating exchange rate regime, it is ill-suited as the main means of reconciling inflation and competitiveness objectives."\par \par \uc2 After the sharp weakening of the shekel on Monday, and despite a subsequent rally to Wednesday's 3.67 level, traders could feel the Bank of Israel might be less inclined to lean against shekel strength at this level.\par \par \uc2 After all, the IMF said Israel needs to tighten monetary policy further and curb an overheating housing market.\par \par \uc2 LEVIATHAN\par \par \uc2 Another factor could contribute to a stronger shekel.\par \par \uc2 The discovery of the Leviathan offshore natural gas field could transform Israel's long-term energy security. [ID:nLDE6BT0FS]\par \par \uc2 Leviathan is estimated to have 16 trillion cubic feet (450 billion cubic metres) of gas. Nearby Tamar was the largest gas find in the world in 2009, at 8.4 trillion cubic feet.\par \par \uc2 While it will take some years before both projects come onstream, the combination of natural resources and Israel's high-tech industries could be attractive to international investors and ultimately boost the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Taking a punt on the shekel is undoubtedly high-risk but it may be worth a tentative second look.\par \par \uc2 Biography of author [ID:nL9197090]\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-SHEKEL (\b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  COLUMN)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|O|OIL|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|PCM|PEN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110205e7220006w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
