\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Israel \highlight\uc2  buys $600 mln to check shekel\b0\par\par\uc2 327 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2010\par 10:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds updated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  figure, quotes, official rate)\par \par \uc2 TEL AVIV, Oct 7 (Reuters) - The Bank of Israel, which raised key interest rate last week, stepped up the pace of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem gains in the shekel <ILS=> on Thursday, buying at least $600 million of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reached a fresh two-year high against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The official rate was fixed at 3.5910 per dollar -- its highest since Oct. 7, 2008 -- compared with Wednesday's rate of 3.6010.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been aggressive today," a dealer at \uc2 Israel Discount Bank\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 "Foreign banks keep on selling (dollars)," he said, though the selling slowed down after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Israel began buying early in the morning when the shekel was at 3.5730.\par \par \uc2 In all of September the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $699 million of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Bank of Israel Governor Stanley Fischer said on Sunday much of the decline in dollar-shekel stems from global dollar weakness and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is determined to prevent the exchange rate from moving too rapidly.\par \par \uc2 "There is no doubt that without \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the shekel would be much stronger," Fischer said, adding it was important to ensure exporters are not harmed since exports comprise more than 40 percent of Israel's economic activity. [ID:nLDE6920AS]\par \par \uc2 With surging housing prices threatening to bring about a spike in inflation, the Bank of Israel raised its key rate by a quarter-point to 2 percent last week. It was the second such move in three months and sixth since August 2009.\par \par \uc2 Analysts forecast at least one more rate hike by year-end and the key rate is expected to top 3 percent in the next year.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Tova Cohen; Editing by John Stonestreet)\par \par \uc2 SHEKEL-\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|MD|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101007e6a7000j3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
