\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Israel \highlight\uc2  shekel strong after rate hike,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 676 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 2010\par 15:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Near 8-1/2 month highs after Monday's 25 bp hike\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buys dollars to stem shekel appreciation\par \par \uc2 * House prices seen rising further, adding to inflation\par \par \uc2 * C.Bank focused on shorter-term econ factors - analyst\par \par \uc2 (Adds c.bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , closing prices)\par \par \uc2 By Tova Cohen\par \par \uc2 TEL AVIV, Sept 28 (Reuters) - The Israeli shekel <ILS=> ended close to multi-month highs on Tuesday in the face of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem its rise, a day after the bank raised interest rates as part of efforts to keep inflation in check.\par \par \uc2 The shekel's official rate was set at 3.6770 per dollar, setting a new 8-1/2 month high for the daily fixing and compared with a traded rate of 3.6650 after the rate rise was announced on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened to 3.682 after the fixing as the Bank of Israel bought $250 million to counter its appreciation, which is hurting exports.\par \par \uc2 The rate increase, by 25 basis points to 2 percent, was largely expected by the market, though Finance Minister Yuval Steinitz had urged the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Sunday not to raise rates to avoid stifling the economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 An analyst said the tightening showed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was focused on the economy's near-term prospects. The bank on Tuesday lowered its 2011 GDP growth estimate, after raising its forecast for 2010 on Monday. [ID:nLDE68R114]\par \par \uc2 Higher vegetable prices are likely to push up the consumer price index in September, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will look primarily at currently soaring house prices to determine the next interest rate move, said Amir Kahanovich, chief economist at the Clal Finance brokerage.\par \par \uc2 "If the situation continues like it was in August and September, when housing prices kept rising, inflationary expectations are up and stocks are gaining, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have to raise rates again," Kahanovich said.\par \par \uc2 There is a more than 50 percent chance of a rate rise at the end of November, he said, but an October increase is less likely.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is looking more at the short term. They raised their forecast for 2010 and this is more important to them right now. The growth in 2011 of 3.8 percent will still be rapid.\par \par \uc2 "Growth is still strong and negative real interest rates aren't appropriate for this growth," he said, adding that the long-term forecasts were problematic as it was difficult to forecast long-term global trade trends.\par \par \uc2 An \uc2 Israel Discount Bank\uc2  dealer said the shekel dip "looks like a normal correction, but a lot will depend on the Bank of Israel."\par \par \uc2 BONDS, SHARES FLAT\par \par \uc2 Government bond prices <0#ILGOI=TA> edged down 0.1 percent.\par \par \uc2 The blue chip Tel Aviv 25 index <.TA25> was flat. "The rate hike was expected and in days leading up to the move the market rose strongly," said a Tel Aviv equities trader.\par \par \uc2 Kahanovich said bonds linked to the consumer price index were falling across the board as the Bank of Israel's move will likely lead to a decline in inflation expectations.\par \par \uc2 Some market players thought the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not raise rates this month in light of the shekel's recent rise. The Bank of Israel has bought dollars several times this month to try to stem the shekel's gain.\par \par \uc2 The bank said on Monday that inflation, an annual 1.8 percent in August, was expected to reach 2.5 percent in the next year -- near the top of an official 1-3 percent target -- with the interest rate likely to gradually rise to 2.7 percent, according to a consensus of the bank's economists.\par \par \uc2 "This will be a game of cat and mouse," the dealer said. "The market will wait for another rate hike. If the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raises the rate two months in a row that would be a lot."\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Tim Pearce, John Stonestreet)\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL-RATES/MARKETS (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|MD|E|RBN|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100928e69s000fx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
