\par\par \b \uc2 PREVIEW-Bank of Israel seen holding rates\b0\par\par\uc2 404 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Mai 2010\par 14:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * WHAT: Israel monetary policy decision\par \par \uc2 * WHEN: Monday, May 24, 5:30 pm (1430 GMT) * REUTERS FORECAST: 10 of 15 analysts polled expect short-term borrowing rate to stay on hold at 1.5 percent. Five analysts see a quarter-point rate increase to 1.75 percent.\par \par \uc2 FACTORS TO WATCH\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Israel is committed to a gradual tightening of monetary policy as the economy continues to rebound and inflation expectations remain high.\par \par \uc2 Governor Stanley Fischer surprised some analysts by leaving the key rate unchanged on April 26 after a quarter-point hike in March. Fischer has raised the key rate four times since August, by one percentage point in total.\par \par \uc2 The consumer price index rose by a higher-than-expected 0.9 percent in April from March, but the annual inflation rate slipped to 3 percent from 3.2 percent, at the top of an official 1 to 3 percent target range.\par \par \uc2 Analysts predict inflation will slip below 2 percent for 2010 but see annual inflation of about 2.5 to 3 percent over the next 12 months.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, the economy continues to rebound although growth slowed in the first quarter to an annualised 3.3 percent, from a 4.8 percent expansion in the final three months of 2009 and a 3.6 percent rise in the third quarter.\par \par \uc2 MARKET REACTION\par \par \uc2 In keeping rates unchanged a month ago, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cautioned that rapid rate increases could put too much appreciation pressure on the shekel, potentially damaging exports. [ID:nLDE64916Y]\par \par \uc2 However, the shekel is now moving in the opposite direction. It has weakened significantly against the dollar <ILS=> in recent sessions, hitting a five-month low of 3.82 on Thursday as the dollar has appreciated sharply versus the euro.\par \par \uc2 The euro <EURILS=>, however, has fallen by some 8 percent against the shekel in the past month and was quoted at 4.7 on Thursday, close to an 18-month low of 4.65 reached last week.\par \par \uc2 To keep the shekel from appreciating too much, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  has continued to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the open market. It bought $2.5 billion of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in April and a yet to be disclosed amount so far in May. (Reporting by Steven Scheer; Editing by Susan Fenton)\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL-RATES/PREVIEW (URGENT)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|MD|RNP|DNP    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100520e65k001pe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
