\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Israel cenbank buys over $500 mln of  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 , shekel dips\b0\par\par\uc2 By Steven Scheer   \par \uc2 488 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 April 2010\par 10:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, official rates, dealer comments)\par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, April 14 (Reuters) - The Bank of Israel bought more than $500 million of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the open market on Wednesday, dealers said, pushing the shekel weaker against the dollar <ILS=> and euro <EURLS=>.\par \par \uc2 Dealers at large Israeli banks said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought between $500 million and $600 million as the shekel remained too strong for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The shekel jumped after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its key short-term borrowing rate by on March 28 -- its fourth such move since last August to combat high inflation expectations.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, is opposed to a stronger shekel on grounds that it hurts exporters at a time when the economy is recovering from a recession.\par \par \uc2 "There was definitely some pretty aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  today -- larger than what we have seen the last few days," said a dealer at \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  Discount Bank\uc2 . "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed the market (dollar and euro) higher."\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Israel bought an estimated $150 million on Tuesday. Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  almost daily the past two weeks in small amounts of $50-$200 million a day. They believe the Bank of Israel has bought some $1.5 billion so far this month.\par \par \uc2 The first round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday morning came as the dollar weakened to below 3.69 shekels and as the euro neared 5 shekels.\par \par \uc2 "They want to make a point that they won't let the shekel strengthen too much and below 3.70 to the dollar and 5 euros are too low for them," said a dealer at Bank Leumi.\par \par \uc2 The shekel was fixed at 3.7050 per dollar, a decline of 0.6 percent from Tuesday after reaching an intraday low of 3.717. It was fixed down 0.8 percent at 5.0468 per euro after reaching nearly 5.07 during the day.\par \par \uc2 The Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved back to 3.699 per dollar and 5.035 to the euro in late trading.\par \par \uc2 Dealers believe the Bank of Israel is trying to defend the 3.70 per dollar level.\par \par \uc2 "There is constant pressure on the downside by local players and foreign banks and is eased only by the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said the Discount dealer.\par \par \uc2 "Once they (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) are out of the market the pressure is constant," said the dealer, noting sales of dollars have been heavy.\par \par \uc2 The Globes financial daily reported that Citibank has been the most active foreign bank in selling dollars.\par \par \uc2 Next for the market is the consumer price index from March. The CPI, due late on Thursday, is expected to show a 0.2 percent increase from February but its annual rate looks to dip to 3.2 percent. [ID:nLDE63D17T]\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Toby Chopra)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ISRAEL\b0 \highlight\uc2 -SHEKEL/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|MD|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100414e64e000hc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
