\par\par \b \uc2 Israel c.bank has "green light" to buy  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  -finmin\b0\par\par\uc2 355 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 April 2010\par 15:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, April 8 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market has the full backing of the government, Finance Minister Yuval Steinitz said in an interview published on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Israel's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for two years in a bid to prevent the shekel from appreciating too much against the dollar <ILS=> and euro <EURILS=> and hurting exports, which are some 40 percent of economic activity.\par \par \uc2 "The Bank of Israel has a green light from my point of view to continue to buy foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if it needs to," Steinitz told the Maariv newspaper.\par \par \uc2 "I don't want to tell the governor (Stanley Fischer) when and where to stop."\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Israel last August halted a more than one-year programme of buying $100 million a day of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  and instead decided it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on days of "unusual developments" in the market.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had initially set a target of reaching as much as $44 billion in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves but they rose to $62 billion in March.\par \par \uc2 "The current level of $62 billion in reserves is not high given Israel's geopolitical situation and the global economic storm which in my estimate is not yet over."\par \par \uc2 Buoyed by a rapidly recovering economy and the Bank of Israel's fourth short-term interest rate increase since last August on March 28, the shekel gained 0.2 percent to 3.6990 on Thursday versus the dollar and 0.7 percent against the euro to 4.9247, a fresh 17-month high.\par \par \uc2 Since then, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought $50-$200 million of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a number of days to keep the shekel from appreciating.\par \par \uc2 Steinitz rejected calls for Israel to impose taxes on capital flows as a means of limiting speculators selling dollars.\par \par \uc2 "I do not support going back 10-20 years and impose barriers on foreign trade and raw materials," he said.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Steven Scheer; editing by Stephen Nisbet)\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL-FINMIN/CENBANK|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|MD|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100408e648000zl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
