\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Bank of Israel raises key rate 25 bps to 1.5 pct\b0\par\par\uc2 646 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2010\par 16:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * First increase since December\par \par \uc2 * 6 of 14 economists in poll had forecast correctly\par \par \uc2 * Bk of Israel says monetary policy still expansionary\par \par \uc2 (Adds comments from \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  statement, analysts)\par \par \uc2 By Steven Scheer\par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, March 28 (Reuters) - The Bank of Israel raised its key short-term borrowing rate <ILINR=ECI> by a quarter point to 1.5 percent on Sunday, its first increase since December, to combat inflationary pressures as the economy recovers.\par \par \uc2 Six of 14 economists polled by Reuters had predicted a quarter-point increase, with eight expecting no change.\par \par \uc2 "The current increase is made against the background of growth that continues to become more firmly based, inflation expectations that are close to the upper limit of the (1-3 percent) target inflation range, and the rise in asset prices," the Bank of Israel said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 "However, monetary policy continues to be expansionary, even after this increase," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  added.\par \par \uc2 The decision was made a day earlier than usual due to the seven-day Jewish festival of Passover, which begins on Monday at sundown. Israeli financial markets will not be able to react until Wednesday, when markets reopen for a shortened session.\par \par \uc2 Markets were already closed on Sunday at the time of the rates decision, which was the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fourth quarter-point move since August.\par \par \uc2 Analysts had been largely split over the prospects of a rate hike, especially since an increase would tend to support a stronger shekel <ILS=> <EURILS=>, something the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been trying to fight by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 "It was a correct decision," said Rafi Gozlan, economist at Leader Capital Markets. "A rate hike at this time sends a determined message against the latest rise in inflation expectations, thus preventing unnecessary future rate hikes."\par \par \uc2 Consumer prices fell by 0.3 percent in February from January to push annual inflation down to a rate of 3.6 percent, still above an official 1-3 percent target. The CPI had fallen a bigger-than-expected 0.7 percent in January.\par \par \uc2 INFLATION EXPECTATIONS\par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  noted inflation expectations for the next 12 months were on average at 2.6 percent. It added that annual inflation is expected to move back within the target range in a month.\par \par \uc2 "It seems as if the governor (Stanley Fischer) gave more weight to the higher inflation expectations than the recent negative CPIs," said Dan Ron, vice president of investment at the Tachlit investment house.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the key lending rate three times in the second half of 2009 on concerns of rising inflation pressures, which started to ease early in 2010.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Israel said in its statement that it was in a process of gradually returning the interest rate to a more "normal" level that was intended to return inflation to its target -- and "keep it there" -- while contributing to the further recovery of economic activity.\par \par \uc2 Israel's economy grew an annualised 4.9 percent in the fourth quarter and 0.7 percent for all of 2009. It is forecast to grow at least 3.5 percent in 2010. The Bank of Israel said uncertainty remained regarding the strength of the expansion.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reiterated the path of rate increases will be determined by inflation, global and domestic growth and the pace of rate increases globally.\par \par \uc2 "Despite today's rate increase, real rates are still negative and too low in comparison to the pace of the economic recovery," Ron said.\par \par \uc2 "The process of rate hikes is not over," he said, adding much depended on upcoming CPIs and the U.S. Federal Reserve. (Additional reporting by Tova Cohen, Ari Rabinovitch, editing by Will Waterman)\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL-RATES/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|MD|BNX|RNP|DNP    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100328e63s00093\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
