\par\par \b \uc2 Israel cbank buys  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  as euro-shekel at 16-month low\b0\par\par\uc2 172 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2010\par 11:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, March 24 (Reuters) - The Bank of Israel likely bought as much as $100 million of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday as the euro reached a 16-month low against the shekel <EURILS=>, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 One dealer at a large Israeli bank said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought when the euro fell below 5 per shekel for the first time since November 2008.\par \par \uc2 The purchases, the dealer said, were made through brokers, making it difficult to give an exact amount.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought small amounts of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  a number of times this month to prevent the shekel from strengthening too much against the euro and dollar <ILS=>, as a strong shekel tends to weigh on exports.\par \par \uc2 The shekel was trading at 4.9970 per euro compared with an official rate of 5.0475 on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Steven Scheer; editing by Patrick Graham)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ISRAEL\b0 \highlight\uc2 -SHEKEL/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|MD|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100324e63o000l0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
