\par\par \b \uc2 Bank of Israel buys $50-$100 mln of  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  -dealers\b0\par\par\uc2 313 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2010\par 15:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, March 15 (Reuters) - The Bank of Israel bought between $50 million and $100 million of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday, as the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  resumed its appreciation, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  entered the market when the dollar-shekel <ILS=> exchange rate reached about 3.7050 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 "It wasn't a significant amount," said a Bank Leumi dealer.\par \par \uc2 But it was enough to move the shekel back below 3.71.\par \par \uc2 The shekel was fixed at 3.7150 per dealer -- its strongest level since Feb. 3 -- up from 3.7180 on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Israel had bought about $130 million of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  last Thursday to curb the shekel's gains. Some 40 percent of economic activity is exports and a strong shekel tends to weigh on exports.\par \par \uc2 The shekel had held between 3.75 and 3.80 to the dollar since Feb. 5 but started to appreciate in the middle of last week on signs that Bank of Israel Governor Stanley Fischer will stay for a second term.\par \par \uc2 Dealers noted that since the dollar did not succeed in appreciating players sold the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Fischer said last week the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sought to stop being a player in the market but said the bank would halt \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  once global markets stabilise.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  last August halted a more than one-year programme of buying $100 million a day of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , shifting to a policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  when it saw unusual movements in the market.\par \par \uc2 It bought just $209 million of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  in February after buying $1.56 billion in January, when the shekel rose to a 15-month peak of 3.66 versus the dollar.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Steven Scheer; Editing by Ron Askew)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ISRAEL\b0 \highlight\uc2 -SHEKEL/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|M|D|MD|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100315e63f0012f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
