\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Israel FX intervention \highlight\uc2  depends on recovery -Fischer\b0\par\par\uc2 By Steven Scheer   \par \uc2 481 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2010\par 10:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TEL AVIV, March 11 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will cut back \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as local and global economic conditions stabilise, Bank of Israel Governor Stanley Fischer said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a small and open country cannot be indifferent to the exchange rate," Fischer said at a conference. "Gradually we will reduce our need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. That is our hope but it very much depends on what happens in Israel and the world."\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Israel last August halted a more than one-year programme of buying $100 million a day of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , shifting to a policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  when it saw unusual movements in the market.\par \par \uc2 It bought just $209 million of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  in February after buying $1.56 billion in January, when the shekel <ILS=> gained to a 15-month peak of 3.66 versus the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Fischer reiterated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in the process of returning short-term interest rates to a more normal level. He noted the pace of rate hikes depended on growth in Israel and the world, inflation and global interest rates.\par \par \uc2 Israel's economy, Fischer said, was starting to return to growth rates seen before the global crisis. The economy grew at least 5 percent a year between 2003 and 2007, and 4 percent in 2008.\par \par \uc2 After a weak first half of 2009, the economy grew an annualised 3.6 percent in the third quarter and 4.9 percent in the fourth quarter of 2009.\par \par \uc2 The economy is forecast to grow around 3.5 percent in 2010.\par \par \uc2 Fischer said global growth was still slow, although Asia with the exception of Japan, was doing well.\par \par \uc2 "In the United States, there are points of weakness but the likely scenario is a continuation of growth at a slower pace than it had been before," he said.\par \par \uc2 The major worry for the global economy remains Europe, Fischer said. He pointed to Greece's debt problems and failed attempts so far to bail out the country.\par \par \uc2 Fischer's five-year term as governor ends next month and Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu has decided to ask him to stay on for another term though a formal offer has yet to be made.\par \par \uc2 Fischer is hinging his decision on final approval of a new law that would reform the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policymaking, such as setting up a board of governors.\par \par \uc2 The plan on Wednesday was approved by parliament's finance committee [ID:nLDE6291N6] but still needs approval from the plenum.\par \par \uc2 "We hope in the next week it will pass," Fischer said. "The new law will make the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  more modern with targets more appropriate for the 21st century."\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Toby Chopra)\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL-FISCHER/|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|MD|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100311e63b000tk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
