\par\par \b \uc2 DAVOS-UPDATE 1-Israel's Fischer hopes to phase out  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  action\b0\par\par\uc2 564 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Januar 2010\par 09:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Fischer hopes to phase out \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  * 2010 inflation likely to be below 2.3-2.7 pct estimates\par \par \uc2  * Israel rates to be normal when global interest rates rise\par \par \uc2  By Krista Hughes and Natsuko Waki\par \par \uc2  DAVOS, Switzerland, Jan 28 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hopes to phase out \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the shekel market as the world economy returns to normal, Governor Stanley Fischer said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2  Speaking to Reuters Insider television at the World Economic Forum in Davos, Fischer also said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not defending any particular level of the shekel <ILS=>.\par \par \uc2  "We hope this is part of (the) transition out of extraordinary measures we took during the global meltdown during which we bought dollars daily. We've \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  since then if the market moved rapidly from what we regard (as) its fundamentals," Fischer said.\par \par \uc2  "We hope this will phase out as the situation returns to normal."\par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel last August halted a more than one-year programme of buying $100 million a day of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and instead said it would buy only on days of "unusual movements".\par \par \uc2  After no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in November and buying a minimal amount in December, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  some seven times so far in January -- the last coming a week ago -- as the shekel <ILS=> has appreciated against the dollar and euro.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has helped weaken the shekel to a rate of 3.73 per dollar from a 15-month peak of 3.66 earlier this month.\par \par \uc2  "We are not going to defend any particular value of the shekel. You can't forever stand against the market," Fischer said. "We go with our judgment of whether the market is right. We are a long way from where we were a few months ago."\par \par \uc2  INFLATION\par \par \uc2  Fischer said buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not inflationary. "We sterilise it so it doesn't affect money supply," he said.\par \par \uc2  Inflation reached a rate of 3.9 percent in 2009. Forecasts for 2010 range from 2.3 to 2.7 percent but Fischer said it would "probably be on the lower side" although it is volatile since it is influenced by external factors such as oil prices.\par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel on Monday held its key short-term borrowing rate at 1.25 percent after raising it by a quarter-point in August, November and December. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said rates would gradually return to "normal".\par \par \uc2  "I think we will start returning to normal when other central banks start raising interest rates," Fischer said. "We're all waiting for central banks of leading countries to raise interest rates."\par \par \uc2  He said central bankers were gradually withdrawing the large amount of monetary stimulus. "The last thing they will do is to raise interest rates, probably," Fischer said.\par \par \uc2  He also said while Israel lowered its public debt burden to about 77 percent of gross domestic product from above 100 percent in five years, a similar move over the next five years was doubtful. \par \par \uc2  "We can probably do it by the end of the decade for sure if (the economy) continues to grow," he said. "We would like to go to something like 60 percent."  (Writing by Steven Scheer, editing by Mike Peacock)  \par \par \uc2 DAVOS/FISCHER (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|MD|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100128e61s000td\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
