\par\par \b \uc2 Shekel weakens vs dollar, cenbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  seen\b0\par\par\uc2 383 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Januar 2010\par 15:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, Jan 20 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's shekel <ILS=> slipped 0.4 percent against the dollar to a nearly two-week low, as dealers said the Bank of Israel bought about $100 million of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "It was not a very large sum," said a dealer at Bank Leumi.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the sixth by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far in 2010, dealers said, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  attempts to stem an appreciation of the shekel against the dollar and euro.\par \par \uc2 A dealer at \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  Discount Bank\uc2  said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had less impact on dollar-shekel than the dollar's more than 1 percent rise against the euro.\par \par \uc2 The shekel's official rate was fixed at 3.7040 per dollar -- its weakest level since Jan. 8 -- compared with 3.69 on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 In trading after the fixing, the shekel weakened to 3.71.\par \par \uc2 The shekel gained as much as 3 percent to reach 3.66 per dollar last week. Dealers have said foreign banks and hedge funds sold large amounts of dollars when they opened their books for the new year.\par \par \uc2 Earlier on Wednesday, the Organisation for Economic Co-\b \highlight22\uc2 Operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Development called on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  "as soon as possible", saying such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could counter interest rate increases that aim to combat inflation. [ID:nLDE60I0VD]\par \par \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Stanley Fischer told reporters that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a temporary measure.\par \par \uc2 "We describe \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a step we hope to stop when we get out of the crisis," Fischer said. "I hope we get to a situation like that. As long as there are differences in interest rates in the world this is an abnormal situation."\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Israel last August halted a more than one-year programme of buying $100 million a day of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and instead said it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on days of "unusual movements".\par \par \uc2 Such purchases have fallen sharply since August but the shekel's appreciation since the start of the year has the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  worried since a stronger shekel tends to hurt exports -- some 45 percent of Israel's economic activity.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Steven Scheer; editing by Patrick Graham)\par \par \uc2 SHEKEL-\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 /|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|MD|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100120e61k0012c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
