\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Israel shekel up 0.9 pct vs dollar to 15-month peak\b0\par\par\uc2 366 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 2010\par 14:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, dealer comments)\par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, Jan 11 (Reuters) - Israel's shekel <ILS=> gained 0.9 percent to its highest official rate since October of 2008 on Monday, as foreign banks continued to dump dollars.\par \par \uc2 The shekel was fixed at 3.6830 to the dollar -- its strongest level since Oct. 15, 2008 -- from 3.7180 on Friday.\par \par \uc2 So far in 2010, the shekel has gained some 2.5 percent versus the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "It's mostly foreign banks selling dollars," said a dealer at \uc2 Israel Discount Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Dealers said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market on Monday, after buying dollars in three sessions last week when the exchange rate moved rapidly from 3.7750 at the end of 2009 towards 3.70.\par \par \uc2 Dealers estimate the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought as much as $500 million of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week to try and prop up the ailing dollar versus the shekel. But unlike similar episodes during the summer, the \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  did little to halt the dollar's decline.\par \par \uc2 Since the beginning of the year, foreign banks have dominated the market, taking on short dollar positions against the shekel after sitting on the sidelines during December.\par \par \uc2 The dollar hit a three-month low versus the euro on Monday, but global dollar weakness only partly explains the weak dollar-shekel.\par \par \uc2 Israel's economy has emerged far more quickly from a recession than anticipated, growing an estimated 0.5 percent in 2009 on the heels of a strong second half. That had prompted the Bank of Israel earlier on Monday to raise its 2010 economic growth estimate to 3.5 percent from 2.5 percent. [ID:nLDE60A0IV]\par \par \uc2 The fast rebound, largely due to expected gains in growth of exports and consumer spending, has led to three quarter-point short-term interest rate increases by the Bank of Israel.\par \par \uc2 Minutes of discussions from the last move on Dec. 28 showed most policymakers supported Bank of Israel Governor Stanley Fischer's decision. [ID:nLDE60A0ZZ].\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Steven Scheer; Editing by Ron Askew)\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL-SHEKEL/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|MD|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100111e61b000yl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
