\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Shares hover at highs; Iceland debt costs rise\b0\par\par\uc2 770 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 2010\par 13:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Emerging shares hover at 17-month highs\par \par \uc2 * Icelandic debt insurance costs spike up on Icesave veto\par \par \uc2 * Romania's leu up despite rate cut; lira and rand off highs\par \par \uc2 By Sebastian Tong\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Jan 6 (Reuters) - Emerging shares eked out gains on Wednesday to hover at their highest levels in over a year but Icelandic debt premiums spiked higher after the island state's president rejected a bill to compensate British and Dutch savers for money lost from the collapse of Icelandic banks.\par \par \uc2 Most emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  retreated from recent multi-week highs though Romania's leu defied a surprise interest rate cut by its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to advance to its strongest level in more than six months.\par \par \uc2 Risk appetite is holding ahead of the release of key U.S. jobs data on Friday, allowing the Philippines and Turkey to tap global bond markets in the first trading week of the year.\par \par \uc2 Figures showing the euro zone's services sector expanding at its fastest pace in over two years in December helped offset persistent investor concerns over Greece's parlous fiscal state. [ID:nLDE6050GG] [ID:nSGE60509G]\par \par \uc2 "Risk appetite is not very strongly entrenched...The main thing that people are looking towards is Friday's payrolls. If they are positive, we may see more risk appetite for the next few weeks. If we get a negative surprise, it could turn," said Beat Siegenthaler, chief strategist emerging markets at \uc2 TD Securities\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The benchmark emerging equities index <.MSCIEF> was up 0.3 percent at 1205 GMT, staying aloft at 17-month peaks but several key bourses had slipped from the multi-month highs reached earlier in the week.\par \par \uc2 Polish <.WIG20> and Hungarian shares <.BUX> retreated after hitting 16-month peaks in the previous session while Israeli shares <.TA25> eased after reaching two-year highs on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Turkish shares <.XU100> slipped 0.3 percent but continued to hover at one-year highs.\par \par \uc2 However, South African stocks <.JTOPI> firmed to cling onto their highest levels in over 16 months while Romanian shares <.BETI> inched 0.5 percent up to six-week highs.\par \par \uc2 ICELAND, ROMANIA\par \par \uc2 Investors took profit on recent gains in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the lira <TRY=> and the rand <ZAR=>, knocking both \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  down from Tuesday's 10-week highs against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The lira's weakness was also blamed on Turkey's $2 billion 30-year bond sale, which was said to renew investor doubts over the country's prospects for sealing a new loan accord with the International Monetary Fund (IMF). [ID:nLDE6050DD]\par \par \uc2 A global bond sale by the Philippines is also reportedly seeing strong investor interest. [ID:nTOE60503V]\par \par \uc2 Emerging sovereign debt spreads tightened five basis points to trade at 269 bps over U.S. Treasuries.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's shekel <ILS=> was flat the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reportedly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the unit from advancing past a nine-week high on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Romania's leu <EURRON=> rose 0.5 percent to reach its strongest level against the euro in over half a year, boosted by euro sales by local banks seeking to reduce hard-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  provisions from last year.\par \par \uc2 Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's consensus defying move on Tuesday to cut its key interest rate by 50 bps, the unit is expected to hold firm.\par \par \uc2 "We look for another 50 bps cut next month and do not expect much pressure on the leu considering reports of M&A activity and expectations that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to cap the downside," said \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  in a research note. Meanwhile, the move by Iceland's president on Tuesday to force a referendum on a bill to repay Britain and the Netherlands more than $5 billion lost by the collapse of Icelandic banks continued to push up the cost of insuring the island state's sovereign debt. Credit default swaps to insure Icelandic debt for five years shot up over 30 bps from the previous close to trade at around 479 bps, according to CMA DataVision.\par \par \uc2 Fitch cut Iceland's credit rating to "junk" status while fellow ratings agency \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  warned of a downgrade. [ID:nLDE6040YB]\par \par \uc2 "The risk now is that this whole issue will remain unresolved for another half year or full year. If the bill is refused in the referendum, Iceland will have to go back to negotiating with the UK and the Netherlands, they can forget about EU membership or the IMF programme," said \uc2 TD Securities\uc2 ' Siegenthaler. (Additional reporting by Carolyn Cohn; editing by Chris Pizzey)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-EMERGING|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100109e6160007k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
