\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Israel cbank should phase out unconventional steps-IMF\b0\par\par\uc2 By Steven Scheer   \par \uc2 688 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Dezember 2009\par 10:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds Bank of Israel governor, Finance Minister comments)\par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, Dec 14 (Reuters) - The International Monetary Fund on Monday called on \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  to phase out unconventional monetary policies and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  gradually as interest rates rise further.\par \par \uc2 In its preliminary report on Israel's economy, the fund said policymakers had kept economic damage from the financial crisis "mild" but urged the government to cut public debt.\par \par \uc2 It said interest rate increases to stop inflation rising as the economy recovers from a recession were "appropriate".\par \par \uc2 "As the appropriate monetary stance tightens and the policy rate rises, so the role of unconventional measures in pursing monetary policy objectives should be reduced," the IMF said.\par \par \uc2 "As recommended globally, withdrawal from 'unconventional measures' -- notably \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- should be phased."\par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  in August ended a more than one-year programme of buying $100 million of dollars a day, replacing it with a plan to buy on days of "unusual movements". It has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since late October.\par \par \uc2 The move to "discretionary" \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was appropriate for the transitional period since it maintains the option should it "prove necessary to secure a sufficiently accommodative stance of monetary policy", the IMF said.\par \par \uc2 But it warned this transitional phase "risks compromising the clarity of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's objectives".\par \par \uc2 "To restore the free floating regime, discretionary \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be formally terminated when the policy rate is well above its effective floor on a sustained basis," the fund added.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in late November raised its key lending rate by a quarter-point to 1 percent, its second such move since August as inflation expectations have risen.\par \par \uc2 "We are pleased that the (IMF) mission expresses support of the monetary policy of the Bank of Israel, including the bank's activity in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market so far, since the outbreak of the crisis," Bank of Israel Governor Stanley Fischer said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 FISCAL POLICIES\par \par \uc2 The fund said any further sustained real rise of the shekel would remain a concern. After hitting around 3.7 per dollar, it has eased to 3.78 and has stuck to a narrow range of late.\par \par \uc2 If capital inflows surge, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should not respond by buying dollars. Capital controls and taxes on inflows -- which some government officials have suggested -- would also be inappropriate, the IMF said,\par \par \uc2 The IMF recommended Israel adopt a target to reduce its debt to 70 percent of gross domestic product by the middle of the next decade and 60 percent by 2020. Debt is expected to edge up to 80 percent by the end of 2010.\par \par \uc2 "Public debt needs to come down decisively," it said, noting Israel's exposure to global and geopolitical shocks. The IMF said income tax cuts could hurt debt reduction.\par \par \uc2 The fund said the budget deficit looked to be close to 5 percent of GDP in 2009, below a target of 6 percent. It said boosting spending and breaching fiscal targets were needed during the crisis but a return to ceilings must be re-established.\par \par \uc2 "The government will continue to manage a careful and responsible exit strategy from the crisis, and will support growth and reduction of debt," said Finance Minister Yuval Steinitz. "We intend to prove, in practice, that Israel's growth potential was, and remains, high."\par \par \uc2 Israel weathered the global crisis well and avoided a financial market meltdown, the IMF said, noting it became a safe haven that attracted a sharp increase in net capital inflows.\par \par \uc2 But its medium-term potential growth rate has fallen by 0.5 percentage points to 3 to 3-1/2 percent a year after big reductions of potential output of major economies, the IMF said.\par \par \uc2 It projected 2010 economic growth of as much as 4 percent.\par \par \uc2 "The decline of the rate of potential growth ... as set forth in the report is an indication of the economy's weakness," Fischer said, noting Israel should not become "complacent".\par \par \uc2 IMF-ISRAEL/ (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|MD|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091214e5ce000jq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
