\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Israel \highlight\uc2  cenbank  \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions \highlight\uc2  risk inflation -OECD\b0\par\par\uc2 427 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 2009\par 11:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 PARIS, Nov 19 (Reuters) - The Organisation for Economic Co-\b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Development (OECD) on Thursday said the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk fuelling inflation and hurting policy credibility.\par \par \uc2 In a bid to help keep the shekel <ILS=> from strengthening too much versus the dollar and further damaging exports, the Bank of Israel began buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early 2008.\par \par \uc2 It scrapped a plan -- also aimed at raising foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves -- of buying $100 million a day in August and has since \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market on days of "unusual movements".\par \par \uc2 "The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ... continued \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk bringing additional inflationary pressures and damaging policy credibility and coherence," the OECD said in a report.\par \par \uc2 It bought $1.27 billion of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  in October, down from $1.65 billion in September and above $4 billion in August. Bank of Israel Governor Stanley Fischer said this week he would not stop until he was certain the market is functioning well.\par \par \uc2 The OECD in its report noted that monetary policy is more normalised following a quarter-point rate hike in August.\par \par \uc2 Israel is in the process of becoming a member of the OECD, which officials expect to be completed sometime in 2010.\par \par \uc2 On fiscal policy, the OECD said Israel was relying on short-term measures to reach deficit and spending goals and described scheduled cuts in corporate and personal taxation for 2010 as "untimely".\par \par \uc2 The OECD expects Israel to meet budget deficit targets of 6 percent of GDP in 2009 and 5.5 percent in 2010 but exceed a 3 percent target in 2011.\par \par \uc2 "The temporary tax increases are due to expire at the end of 2010, contributing to uncertainties for the budget balance in 2011," the report said.\par \par \uc2 It added that upside risks to inflation are amplified, saying standard indicators of slack may be inaccurate due to the after-effects of the recent recession on potential output.\par \par \uc2 The OECD projected Israeli GDP growth of zero this year, 2.25 percent in 2010 and 3.25 percent in 2011, with inflation at a 3.3 percent rate next year. The debt-to-GDP ratio looks to rise to 82 percent in 2010 from 78 percent in 2008 and then drop slightly in 2011, the OECD said.\par \par \uc2 "Further increases in the (\b \highlight22\uc2 central) bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy rate are expected with a return to more normal conditions," it said. (Reporting by Steven Scheer; Editing by Andy Bruce)\par \par \uc2 OECD-ISRAEL/|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|MD|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091119e5bj000or\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw77\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1155\pichgoal600
