\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Israel cenbank buys  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  as shekel stays strong\b0\par\par\uc2 By Steven Scheer \par \uc2 475 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Oktober 2009\par 13:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited \par \par \uc2 (Updates with official rates, details of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, Oct 15 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time in nine days, buying as much as $400 million to slow the shekel's <ILS=> appreciation against the globally weak dollar.\par \par \uc2 Dealers at a number of large Israeli banks said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought between $100 million and $400 million of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in various stages during the afternoon.\par \par \uc2 "They came in a few times. It wasn't in one shot," said a dealer with an Israeli bank.\par \par \uc2 The move came hours before a key inflation report is set to be published that could give the market clues on near-term interest rate policy.\par \par \uc2 It also came as the dollar briefly dipped just below 3.70 shekels.\par \par \uc2 For days, the market believed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  should the dollar dip below the 3.70 shekel level.\par \par \uc2 The dollar gained to 3.72 shekels after the buying but the knee-jerk rally quickly ran out of steam.\par \par \uc2 The shekel's official rate was set at 3.7180 per dollar, down 0.2 percent from Wednesday's rate of 3.7090, which was the strongest level since Dec. 18, 2008.\par \par \uc2 After the official rate was set, the shekel gained to 3.7075.\par \par \uc2 A dealer at another large Israeli bank said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not successful since it resulted in "just a 30 minute spike" for the dollar.\par \par \uc2 But with the dollar weak around the world, the Bank of Israel is just trying to keep the shekel from appreciating too fast since a strong shekel tends to hurt Israeli exports, which account for nearly half of economic activity.\par \par \uc2 Exports have already been damaged by the global recession.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market on Oct 6., buying an estimated $200 million of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In August, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  halted a more than year-long programme of buying $100 million a day of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  and instead said it would enter the market on days of unusual activity.\par \par \uc2 At 1630 GMT, the consumer price index for September is due. The CPI is expected to decline 0.1 percent from August and stand 3 percent higher over the past 12 months.\par \par \uc2 High inflation had prompted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise its key short-term borrowing rate by a quarter-point to 0.75 percent in August but easing inflation pressures and inflation expectations led the Bank of Israel to keep rates steady last month.\par \par \uc2 The next monetary policy decision is slated for Oct. 26 and analysts believe another rate hike is possible should the CPI come in above expectations.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Toby Chopra)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ISRAEL\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|MD|DNP \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091015e5af000wp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
