\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Bank of Israel buys $200 mln of  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  -dealers\b0\par\par\uc2 337 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Oktober 2009\par 13:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, dealer comment)\par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, Oct 6 (Reuters) - The Bank of Israel bought as much as $200 million of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in three weeks, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 Dealers at a number of Israeli banks said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the dollar fell below the 3.72 shekel mark.\par \par \uc2 Prior to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the shekel's <ILS=> official rate was set at 3.7330 per dollar, up 0.7 percent from Monday's rate of 3.76.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week will set official rates three hours earlier than usual at about 1030 GMT due to the Jewish Sukkot holiday. Dealers said that due to the holiday, volumes are very low.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases pushed the dollar to 3.76 but dollar setting emerged to move the exchange rate back to 3.7350 in trading in London and New York.\par \par \uc2 A dealer at one large Israeli bank said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was still successful since "it moved the dollar two figures (from 3.7150 to 3.7350) from the day's lows."\par \par \uc2 The shekel is hovering at its strongest level versus the dollar since mid-December of 2008 and the Bank of Israel is trying to keep the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from appreciating further and making exports even less competitive.\par \par \uc2 In August, it halted a more than one-year programme of buying $100 million of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  a day, instead opting to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on days of unusual movements, partly as a means of combating speculators.\par \par \uc2 In data issued on Tuesday, the Bank of Israel said it bought $1.65 billion of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  in September after more than $4 billion in August. [ID:nJEC002013].\par \par \uc2 It last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market on Sept. 16 when dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought at least $200 million of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (Reporting by Steven Scheer; editing by Chris Pizzey)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ISRAEL\b0 \highlight\uc2 -CENBANK/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|MD|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091006e5a6000ps\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
