\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Shekel hits 9-month peak, c.bank buys more  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Joseph Nasr   \par \uc2 550 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2009\par 15:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, Sept 16 (Reuters) - Israel's shekel <ILS=> rose to a nine-month high on Wednesday, prompting the Bank of Israel to buy as much as $200 million in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent further appreciation from harming exports and economic growth.\par \par \uc2 "The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  started \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  (in mid-afternoon), and we estimate they bought around $200 million so far," a dealer at a large Israeli bank told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 The shekel's official rate was set at 3.74 per dollar, its strongest level since Dec. 19, 2008 and a 0.6 percent increase from Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 After closing at 3.76 per dollar on Tuesday, the shekel advanced early in the day to near 3.74, a day after publication of inflation data for August that analysts said would likely prompt the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hike interest rates again next week.\par \par \uc2 The dollar rose to 3.76 shekels in afternoon trading after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but analysts doubt whether the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  can slow the shekel's appreciation in the long term through \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market from time to time since halting last month a programme lasting more than one year during which it bought $100 million a day in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . When it halted that programme, it said it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on days of "unusual movements".\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , seeking to strike a balance between unwinding an expansionary policy in order to fight inflation and avoiding a slowdown in economic recovery, raised its key lending rate by a quarter percentage point on Aug. 24 to 0.75 percent.\par \par \uc2 In data issued after the market closed on Tuesday, Israel's consumer price index rose by 0.5 percent in August, a 3.1 percent increase year-on-year, above an official target of 1 to 3 percent. Analysts said the figure could prompt another quarter-point rate hike on Sept. 24 despite the annual inflation rate falling from a 3.5 percent rate in July.\par \par \uc2 "The steep rise in the CPI and the market's expectation for inflation ... could lead to a hike of 25 basis points and bring the interest rate to 1 percent," Rafael Gozlan, economist at Leader Capital Markets, wrote in a client note.\par \par \uc2 In August the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $4.073 billion in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market, bringing the country's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to $56.4 billion.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Israel expanded its programme once the shekel reached close to 3.74 per dollar in early August. The shekel slumped to 3.93 but the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the past six weeks has gradually gained as the economy has shown signs of recovery and as the dollar has been weak globally.\par \par \uc2 Also on Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said inflation expectations for the next 12 months held steady at 2.4 percent.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, the Central Bureau of Statistics estimated Israel's economy would grow 0.1 percent in 2009. [ID:nLG62347]. The economic recovery pu